eration in solving societal problems, and new forms of multilevel policy. In development policy, the governance concept has also gained relevance in the 1990s, frequently with the contested qualiﬁer “good governance” (20). The more recent notion of “global governance” 278 Biermann· Pattberg Annu. Rev. Environ. Resourc. 2008.33:277-294. Downloaded from arjournals.annualreviews.org by VRIJE UNIVERSITEIT-Amsterdam-Library on 10/20/08. For personal use only.",6,False,SUGGEST_ACCEPT,PENDING,,Full corpus Pass 2 (synonym-expanded) — remaining documents,Explanation/Elaboration,Draft memo: relevant discussion tagged as effectiveness; verify alignment with theme definition and adjust tag if the construct boundary is better captured elsewhere.,b9022f6f22,Global Environmental Governance Taking stock Moving Forward Biermann Pattberg2008,,10.1146/annurev.environ.33.050707.085733
