stage2_pass2full_20260125T233829Z,stage2_pass2full_20260125T233829Z_0000801,False,Greening the United Nations charter_World politics in the anthropocene.pdf,19,Unspecified,governance working paper,TH051,Institutionalism Organizational Analysis,Pass 2 (theme + validated synonym dictionary),"Verbatim paragraph excerpt (PDF text layer), extracted at paragraph boundary","EARTH System **governance working paper** No. 21 | 19 systems, what is now needed is a new constitutional moment to strengthen the overall institutional framework for effective governance of the interaction of human societies with the planetary system. Acknowledgement The author is chair of the Earth System Governance Project and has led in this function several policy assessments in preparation for the 2012 UN Confe","EARTH System **governance working paper** No. 21 | 19 systems, what is now needed is a new constitutional moment to strengthen the overall institutional framework for effective governance of the interaction of human societies with the planetary system. Acknowledgement The author is chair of the Earth System Governance Project and has led in this function several policy assessments in preparation for the 2012 UN Conference on Sustainable Development, involving several dozen senior experts in this field. The present paper draws on these assessments and on numerous fruitful discussions within the Earth System Governance Project, notably at the 2011 Colorado Conference on Earth System Governance (May 2011) and the 2011 Hakone Vision Factory on Earth System Governance (September 2011). However, all opinions expressed, while drawing on collective work and discussions, are solely the responsibility of the author alone. For valuable suggestions and comments on earlier drafts of the present paper, the author is grateful to Aarti Gupta, Philipp Pattberg, Timothy O’Riordan, and Ruben Zondervan.",2,False,SUGGEST_REVIEW,PENDING,,Full corpus Pass 2 (synonym-expanded) — remaining documents,Substantiation/References,Draft memo: relevant discussion tagged as institutionalism organizational analysis; verify alignment with theme definition and adjust tag if the construct boundary is better captured elsewhere.,173fe6145a,Greening the United Nations charter World politics in the anthropocene,,
